    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Operational Interpretation",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 10,
        "x": 14,
        "y": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Edge routing operating signals\n- **Remote Routing Ratio**: sustained growth means SITE/ZONE/REGION choices are no longer safely available; inspect `fallback_reason` logs before changing policy.\n- **Fallback Ratio**: separates normal locality selection from degraded topology selection. `SITE_UNAVAILABLE`, `SITE_ZONE_UNAVAILABLE`, and `LOCAL_UNAVAILABLE` are bounded policy reasons.\n- **Fresh Latency Coverage**: a drop toward zero means Phase 51/52 is increasingly choosing with load-only evidence; investigate latency-signal freshness rather than treating stale samples as truth.\n- **Locality Distribution**: validates that traffic normally stays in the nearest safe tier and shows when it moves outward.\n- **Routing logs** retain backend identity and scores for diagnosis; metrics intentionally do **not** label by backend/request/trace IDs.\n\n**Operator rule:** dashboards explain symptoms; health/circuit/capacity safety remains authoritative. Never relax safety because a dashboard shows a remote or slower route."
      }
    }
